package CanvasNet {
    part def MarkBuilder {
        doc /* The internal MarkBuilder (a sealed class) with IsSupported (true for bar, rect, point, circle, square, rule, and tick) and Build, which reads the mark type (a string or the type of a mark definition), loops over the rows of the DataTable (cancellation polled every 1,024 rows, the scene budget charged for the marks group and each item before it is created), maps the channels x, y, color, fill, stroke, size, and opacity through the scale models (field, value, and datum forms), resolves the mark properties through the ResolvedConfig precedence chain, and creates the SceneRect, SceneSymbol, and SceneRule items of a marks group in the coordinates of the data rectangle: bars, rectangles, and ticks fill the band on a discrete position (at least minBandSize; step minus 2 on a point scale) and are centered with continuousBandSize or thickness on a continuous one, the measure axis runs from the value to zero (or, for a stacked channel and for an x2 or y2 range, from the start to the end), symbols sit at the band center or the value with the size as the area of the bounding box (at the upper end of a stack), and rules are full-width or full-height lines, stems to zero, or segments of a range; Phase 6 draws the stacked layers of the EncodingPlan from the start to the end value of each row, the x2 and y2 secondary channels of bar, rect, and rule marks (a field, a datum, or a pixel value; a row with an invalid end is not drawn), a bar or rect on a binned channel as the span of its bin less binSpacing (bar 1, rect and tick 0) with a half-pixel edge and a minimum of minBandSize, the bin midpoint for point-like marks, and the clip of the data rectangle when the x or y scale has an explicit array domain (unless clip is false); paint follows Vega-Lite (the mark color is the fill of a filled mark and the stroke of an unfilled one, ordinal colors from tableau10, default opacity 0.7 for point, circle, square, and tick). A row with a null, NaN, or non-numeric value on a continuous channel is not drawn. Exceeding MaxSceneItems is a VegaLiteRenderException with the location of the mark, and cancellation is polled every 1,024 rows. Phase 5 gives the constructor an optional RowExpressions (the compiled expressions and the evaluator of the call): the expr references of the drawn view's mark color, fill, stroke, opacity, strokeWidth, and size (point, circle, and square) and of the constant value of the color, fill, stroke, opacity, and size (point, circle, and square) channels are evaluated once per row against the transformed row, a text result being a color and a finite number an opacity, width, or size, any other result leaving the default; conditional encodings and every other expression site are ignored (and reported by the FeatureCatalog). */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/MarkBuilder.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Marks/NamespaceDoc.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Marks/MarkBuilderTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/marks/mark-builder.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/marks/mark-builder.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/marks/mark-builder.yaml */
    }
}
